My Love,

Today marks eleven years since our paths first crossed. Eleven years since a small moment in Wageningen quietly started an _Entdeckungsreise_ - an exploration I dreamed of.

I still smile when I think about how it began. That lunch meeting where we first saw each other - a seemingly ordinary moment. And yet somehow it created just enough familiarity for us to easily talk again a few days later at that party. I didn't know it yet during lunch, but that party evening something shifted in me. _Dat was het moment dat ik oprecht verliefd op je werd_ - with your kind heart, your curiosity about the world, your exploratory vibes, and of course, your smile and positive nature.

I love that we have been travelling together ever since. 

Not only across countries - though we certainly did a fair share of that. Recently I tried to look up what our very first trip together was. I went through my photos and it seems that Stockholm might have been the first real holiday we took together. (Although there is a mysterious gap in my photos in 2015, so maybe I'm missing something!... Do you remember?) But the Sweden trip I remember vividly. Kayaking together through the water around Stockholm Archipelago - discovering the little private islands from the water, quietly gliding along with pure water underneath us. _Heerlijk._ I loved that.

Over the years we have taken so many journeys together. Through rainy mountains, across deserted land, ... but also into our tiny house, and into entirely new chapters of life. Some adventures were big and wild, others small and quiet. But some of my favourite journeys are still the conversations we have had along the way - in bars at night, during long drives, or simply sitting somewhere talking about life with a glass of wine and some not so vegan delicious cheese. _Diese tiefen Gespräche genieße ich in vollen Zügen nach wie vor._

In our vows I once called you my true north. And I still feel that today. When life gets confusing or the path ahead foggy, you are the safe harbour that gently guides me back.

Lately, I feel something beautiful returning again. I am truly proud of you for stepping up your exploring mode again, for searching again, for allowing yourself to discover new directions or at the very least being open to it. I love seeing that spark. And I love that somehow we seem to have more time again - or maybe simply more energy (?) - for the kind of deep conversations that have always been such an important part for me.

And yet I also love the very practical journeys we navigate together. Managing life. Getting things in order. Building our little world step by step. I felt that so strongly while we were figuring out schools for Felien. I was genuinely happy doing that with you - being able to help you in the beginning of the process to bring some structure, to get things started, thinking things through together, visiting schools together, making decisions together, shaping the environment in which our daughter will grow. _Thuis komen doe ik het liefst vol enthousiasme bij jullie twee samen._

Being a parent with you is one of the greatest adventures of my life. I love watching you as a mother. I love building this family together with you. And I love being by your side as your partner. 11 years later... 11 more to come... and hoefully so many more after that...

Sometimes our life together feels like a long expedition. We carry maps, snacks, laughter, chaos, and occasionally the question: “Are we actually doing this right?” But somehow we always find the next path forward. And when storms appear - as they inevitably do on any long journey - I still trust what I promised you: that I will uphold truth, trust, and trouble to never make this journey boring.

And... who knows, hopefully soon another little traveler may join our expedition.

I look forward to that deeply. To welcoming another little human into this strange and beautiful journey we are on together. I will admit that sometimes I also feel a little scared about how we will manage it all. Life already feels full and intense. But the truth is: I do want this journey with you. Parenthood with you has been one of the most beautiful experiences of my life. So don't be mad at me next time I get my doubts... cause I will... it is not that I really doubt it, it is just that I am sometimes scared of the additional pressure and time commitment it will bring - and that I currently manage well and that will be challenged again.

Also... I have to say: the way you recently seduced me into slowing down was very smooooth. Just a candle, a conversation, and gently pulling me away from the laptop. Honestly, that was seduction level 103. I did not stand a chance. And I loved it. 

Mieke, if the last eleven years have taught me anything, it is that the most meaningful journeys are rarely the ones we carefully plan... that anyways is not really us... They are the ones we walk together, discovering the path step by step. You are still the explorer I most want beside me.

For the next mountains.
For the next oceans.
For the next quiet conversations in the middle of the night.
For the next little traveler(s) who may join our path.

Hand in hand, still discovering. And perhaps many years from now we will look back again at this moment and smile - remembering that it all began with a simple lunch in Wageningen, and two people who decided to keep walking in the same direction.

\
_I love you._ \
_Ik hou van je._ \
_Ich liebe dich._

\
Mario 
